# Regression proofs

Proofs to run the checker over, with the verdict each should get.

```bash
lake exe @EXE@ test/regress/<proof>
```

Three verdicts are worth covering, not two:

| verdict | status | what a test here would show |
| ------- | ------ | --------------------------- |
| `correct` | 0 | a refutation the checker accepts |
| `incorrect` | 1 | something it must reject |
| `incomplete` | 2 | a proof it accepts that the semantics does not model |

The third is the one that is easy to forget and most worth having: it is what
keeps `correct` from quietly overstating what the soundness theorem covers.
